---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Newsletter from '../../components/Newsletter.astro';
import NotesToRecord from '../../components/NotesToRecord.astro';
---
<Base title="For veterinary teams" description="An AI documentation assistant built for the keyboard: type rough notes, approve the finished record, generate owner instructions and referral letters from it.">
  <section class="wrap hero hero-split vets-hero">
    <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation assistant · in development</p>
    <h1>You examine. We write it up.<br />You approve.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Type a few rough lines after the consultation. Get a structured, professional record to review. Nothing on the page you didn't write. Then make the owner's instructions, the referral letter and a translation from the same approved record, without typing anything twice.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="#waitlist">Join the early-access list</a> <a class="btn secondary" href="/vets/workspace" style="margin-left:8px">Try the preview</a></p>
    <ul class="chips"><li>GDPR by design</li><li>Hosted in the EU</li><li>Never trains on your data</li><li>Nothing recorded, no microphone</li></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="vets-hero-art"><NotesToRecord lang="en" /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What it looks like</h2>
    <div class="mock" aria-label="Example: notes on the left, generated report on the right">
      <div>
        <div class="h">Your notes</div>
<pre>Luna, Lab, F, 6y
vomiting 3x since yesterday
no diarrhea
reduced appetite, drinking ok
T 39.1
abdomen soft, mild pain
bloods + US done
fluids + antiemetic
recheck 48h</pre>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="h">Consultation report · draft</div>
        <div class="sec">Reason for presentation</div>
        <div>Vomiting 3x since yesterday.</div>
        <div class="sec">History</div>
        <div>Owner reports: no diarrhoea; appetite reduced; drinking ok.</div>
        <div class="sec">Clinical examination</div>
        <div>Temperature 39.1 °C. Abdomen: soft, mild pain.</div>
        <div class="sec">Diagnostics</div>
        <div>Bloods, ultrasound (done). <span class="flag">▲ Missing: results</span></div>
        <div class="sec">Treatment</div>
        <div>Fluids, antiemetic. <span class="flag">▲ Missing: drug, dose, route</span></div>
        <div class="sec">Follow-up</div>
        <div>Recheck 48h.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>Your words, put in order: nothing is paraphrased into something you did not say. The flags are the point. The assistant does not fill gaps with plausible text. It shows you what's missing, you add it or mark it "not recorded", and you approve with one keystroke.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What we commit to</h2>
    <p>We studied more than thirty AI note-taking tools and what vets say about them. These are the answers.</p>
    <ol class="commit">
      <li><b>Nothing on the page you didn't write.</b> No drug, dose, route, number or diagnosis appears unless it is in your notes.</li>
      <li><b>Every sentence shows its source.</b> Click a line in the report and see the note it came from.</li>
      <li><b>Missing information is flagged, never invented.</b> Before you sign, you see what isn't there.</li>
      <li><b>Owner's words stay the owner's words.</b> "Owner reports…" is never turned into your finding.</li>
      <li><b>Patient facts are locked.</b> Species, sex and reproductive status come from the patient record, never from prose.</li>
      <li><b>One approved record, every document.</b> Owner summary with a dose checklist, referral letter, prescription, vaccination entry, consent form and cost estimate come only from what you signed. <a href="/vets/workspace">Switch documents in the preview.</a></li>
      <li><b>Your edits are never lost.</b> Regenerating a section shows a diff and keeps your text.</li>
      <li><b>No recording.</b> Nothing to consent to, nothing to store, no barking-dog problem. It works with a keyboard.</li>
      <li><b>Native German, Italian and English.</b> Owner documents in the owner's language, with medication details copied exactly.</li>
      <li><b>Your data stays in the EU and is never used to train AI.</b> On every plan. <a href="/vets/data">Subprocessors, retention and your rights, in public.</a></li>
      <li><b>Cancel any month.</b> Clear per-vet pricing; nurses and reception are free.</li>
      <li><b>A public quality page.</b> We publish how the assistant is tested, on real document types, with the numbers. <a href="/vets/quality">See the current results.</a></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Works next to your practice software</h2>
    <p>It runs in the browser beside whatever system your clinic uses. After approval, copy the record box by box (S, O, A, P) into your practice software, download it as JSON with the approval details, export a PDF on your letterhead, or print. Direct integrations will follow only through official vendor programmes, never through workarounds.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Review articles for owners</h2>
    <p>Our articles for animal owners are drafts until a practising vet checks and signs them. Your name and registration go on every article you sign, and nothing changes after you sign without a new review. <a href="/vets/review">How reviewing works →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap narrow" id="waitlist" style="margin-top:56px">
    <h2>Early access</h2>
    <p>We're looking for a small number of clinics in Germany, Austria, Switzerland and Italy to test with. If you type your own notes and would like documentation to take less of your evening, leave your email and tick "veterinary professional".</p>
    <Newsletter compact />
    <p style="margin-top:16px"><a href="/vets/research">Read our research on existing tools →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
